cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper
  listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
title: "StaticSBFL: Static Suspiciousness Prediction for Neural Networks"
abstract: >
  Replication package for static suspiciousness prediction: generates and
  trains populations of dense neural networks, measures their hit spectra,
  predicts the Tarantula, Ochiai and D* suspiciousness of every neuron from
  weight statistics and architecture features without executing the model,
  and compares the runtime and memory of the static prediction with dynamic
  hit-spectrum tools.
authors:
